bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_pattern_same_name_class_identity_unchecked_2026_11_27, 0, "Follow-up of interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26 (Fable review 2026-11-27, fixtures t1/t2 under the review scratch neg/src/pkg). JIT match patterns do not check class identity: qa.qa_any(qb_make()) with `case P { x }` matches qb.P in the JIT, and an entry pattern on `P` (imported from qa) or `Q` (alias of qb.P) matches either module instance, while the interpreter rejects the wrong owner (test/fixtures/same_name_class/body/main_alias_neg.spl prints aliasneg pa=3 pb=-1 qa=-1 qb=5 in the interpreter). The two lanes disagree; the JIT needs an owner-identity check (type id compare) in struct patterns. pipeline/module_loader.rs warns on co-compiled same-named classes until this is fixed."

